144-## Design decisions grounded in research
145-
146-- Relaxing music tends to be legato, unaccented, soft (pp–mp), smooth in contour, repetitive, mid-register and thin in texture (web listening study of 293 adults; Conrad et al., *medRxiv* preprint, 2023). The composer’s rules (soft velocities, long releases, stepwise melody, density cap, mid-register lead) follow these findings.
147-- People relax differently: a study that slowed tempo to 45 BPM and softened timbre found two distinct responder profiles (Hernández-Ruiz et al., *Psychology of Music*, 2020). That is why there are five moods and a user tempo control (40–96 BPM).
